																		Happy Mask Man
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/krystal-cipher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6994728); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6994728&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606508089" alt="Krystal_Cipher" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6994728)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/krystal-cipher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6994728); return false;" >Krystal_Cipher</a></span> <span class="odate time_1604794508 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Nov 2020 00:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4813404">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> typical class, containment procedures, description, an origin storyfollowed by some test logs and two interviews, and then, an addendum with a twist and a final interview</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A ceramic mask in a pile of goop that makes people happy by turning them into zombies.<br />
He can change his viscosity at will, flow through any crack water can by dissolving the mask into itself, and his goop will turn into ceramic after a while if it’s separated from him. If he’s given a person who doesn’t have their face covered or inaccessible, he’ll create a mask resembling his own and be intensely compelled to try to force it on them. There’s no anomalous compulsion on the part of the victims. When it’s placed, it permanently turns the victim into basically a happy zombie. I know this sounds a little like 035, but the only similarity is that they’re sentient masks in black goop, nothing else about them, their story, their abilities, and their reasons for being matches.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> an anartist, struck with clinical depression and anxiety, turns themselves into an anomaly designed to mask pain and force happiness upon its victims- a form of suicide without death, leaving behind only a happy shell of a person. Upon being contained, the anomaly makes its first friend in the senior researcher, who is suddenly struck with personal tragedies beyond what she can handle, and knowing that it’s unable to stop itself, forces the anomaly to turn her into a shell. The anomaly explains this in an incident addendum, and it’s explained that it goes a little crazy, before the final addendum: the anomaly has requested to be terminated.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> a short look into happiness vs freedom, depression in art, and what happens when denial finally starts to break. Other themes that come to mind for me are the burden of free will and the consequences of lacking it, the effect a compulsion would really have on an anomaly’s psyche, and the impact of loneliness. If you could be happy forever, but had to lose everything else, would you take that deal?</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I’ve had this character in mind for months, and I’ve been writing him in a different form for years, so I have a full draft ready, but I’m open to changing it.<br />
I did try posting this to the main site already, but it kinda failed. I’ve since fixed it according to the feedback I’ve received.<br />
Also I should note that I’ve experienced depression and suicidal ideation myself and have the foreknowledge to approach the topic respectfully, and of course, intend to.<br />
I’ve edited this post majorly since asking for review the first time. Thank you everyone for your input!</p>

