<p>I have to agree that there are a few too many similarities to 035. At the same time, I sense potential that isn't being expounded upon.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When it’s placed, it permanently turns the person into basically a happy zombie. Because of this, he’s a little lonely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Specifically this section. I think there's a lot of metaphorical potential for masking pain or sadness (literally). I'm not the biggest fan of the force placing, perhaps you switch that to the mask seeking out people that it believes need help.</p>
<p>For your narrative, I would focus on the creator. I do like the freedom vs. happiness concept, and you can connect that to my suggestion above. I would also look into Are We Cool Yet? Connecting this to happiness, many famous artists have gone through bouts of depression or times where they felt unappreciated, maybe this can be the outcome of an artist experiencing this? If you go with this, you want to approach the topic respectively.</p>

