<p>Responding to PM request.</p>
<hr />
<p>So, as it is, there isn't enough information. Allow me to fully elaborate.</p>
<p>I could get behind this idea and it's themes, though there's some things I would trim out. Compulsory effects, for example, are a bit overdone and don't play well with narratives; it's much more exciting if someone is doing something willingly without much coercion from external forces. Same could be said for the liquification effect, as it doesn't really do much else but add an effect to the mask, as fun as it is. That said, I think what is effectively a mask that makes someone uselessly happy could be an interesting avenue to play with, especially if there is a present conflict within the wearer. There's definitely something worth exploring there.</p>
<p>However, there isn't actually an explanation of what is being done with the mask. You touch on it a little bit in the page layout and the central narrative, but there's still basically nothing but a happy mask. I think there could have been more time spent telling us what path the article takes rather than the effects of the item itself because, in the end, the SCP format is a way to tell a story. We're years passed the &quot;magical item list&quot; style of SCP. Most people will be more warmed up to something with a narrative.</p>
<p>Take some time to tell us, briefly, the pieces that make your article's story.</p>

